FINAL ANSWER:
`lib/index.js` is 238 lines with 62 commits, and git shows no renames. Troy Goode wrote it and still owns most of it.

**Who shaped it**
- **Troy Goode** made the first commit on 2013-01-30. He made 29 of the 62 commits, including header lookup, the `origin: false` behavior, strict mode and the CORS-spec cleanup. He also made a commit on 2026-04-10.
- **Simon Mansfield** (2013) made the credentials and `Origin` check fixes. **Damien Klinnert** (2013) made the change that sends `Access-Control-Allow-Methods` only on OPTIONS requests.
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson** made 4 commits in 2017 and is the second-largest contributor to the current code.
- **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades** made 4 commits, plus 1 more under the name `alex94puchades`.
- The rest are single commits from many contributors, in 2013–2018 and one in 2021 (LuisEGR).
- Activity peaked in 2013–2015 (48 commits). It was 8 commits in 2017 and almost none afterward.
- **Fiona Formatter** made the most recent commit, 62628c0 on 2026-04-12 (`style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes`). It is a mechanical reformat.

**Whose code is still in it**

A plain `git blame` credits Fiona Formatter with 214 of 238 lines, because the reformat touched nearly every line. I ignored that commit (`--ignore-rev 62628c0`) to see who wrote the logic. Whitespace-only changes were ignored too (`-w`), and moved lines were followed (`-M -C`).

| Author | Lines |
|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 159 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 22 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (plus `alex94puchades`, 4) | 12 (16 combined) |
| Raymond Feng | 7 |
| max.laverse | 6 |
| LuisEGR | 6 |
| Simon Mansfield | 3 |
| Igor Soarez | 3 |
| Benjamin Eidelman | 3 |
| 10 others | 1–2 each |

Troy Goode wrote about two thirds of the current lines (159 of 238), from 2013 onward. Almost all the rest is small patches from about 18 contributors. Only 2 of Goode's 29 commits are dated after 2013–2015, so the file has been close to stable since 2017.

