FINAL ANSWER:
`lib/index.js` was created by Troy Goode on 2013-01-30 ("first commit"). It has 62 commits and 238 lines today. Troy Goode wrote most of it.

**Who shaped it**
- **Troy Goode** is the original author and the main contributor, with 29 of the first 40 or so commits by author count. In 2013 they built the core: case-insensitive header lookup, `origin: false` disabling CORS, lint fixes, and pausing and resuming the request for async middleware. They also made the 2026-04-10 commit "lib: annotate handlers".
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson** was the maintainer in 2017. They updated eslint (`<email redacted>`) and fixed paren spacing.
- **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades** (alongside `alex94puchades`, which may be the same person under another name) and **Simon Mansfield** each contributed several commits.
- Single-commit contributors include Benjamin Eidelman (a Safari workaround for the default pre-flight response), Tom Arad (the fix for setting `maxAge` to 0), Chima Alaebo (removed an unreachable branch), LuisEGR (removed unused function parameters) and Saad Tazi.
- **Fiona Formatter** made the 2026-04-12 commit that reformatted the file to 4-space indent and double quotes. That commit is formatting only.

**Whose code is still there**

I ran `git blame` with whitespace changes ignored and with the reformat commit skipped (`--ignore-rev 62628c0`). The count is of the 238 lines:

| Author | Lines |
|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 159 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 22 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 12 |
| Raymond Feng | 7 |
| max.laverse | 6 |
| LuisEGR | 6 |
| alex94puchades | 4 |
| Simon Mansfield | 3 |
| Igor Soarez | 3 |
| Benjamin Eidelman | 3 |
| Saad Tazi | 2 |
| Mathias Buus | 2 |

The list is cut at 12 names. Those lines add up to 229, so about 9 more lines belong to authors not shown.

Without `--ignore-rev`, blame gives Fiona Formatter 32 lines. That is only because of the quote-style changes. Those lines are Troy's and others' original code.

I did not check which of Troy's 159 lines date from 2013 and which from the 2026 annotations. I also did not check whether the same person appears under more than one name or email.

